      {
        "quote": "At €40.99 (or even €61.99 for the brave souls who wanted a few days of early access), Halloween: The Game is a very sour treat—one that sometimes feels like a bad prank. Between its deplorable technical polish and its riddled-with-holes game design, Illfonic’s new asymmetrical horror game gives the impression that no lessons have been learned since the days of Friday the 13th. Much like the cheap exploitation slashers of the 1980s, the genre seems doomed to navel-gazing and stagnation, appealing only to a handful of enthusiasts undeterred by rough edges, poor special effects, and ham-fisted gore. That’s fair enough. It’s even fun at times. But it’s hard to truly recommend to the average player.",
        "score": 40,
